course: dictionary
lesson: 12453
title: A formal word for going to the toilet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound formal, like they belong in a doctor's office or a science book. Read the words around them to find the meaning. «Every animal must defecate to get rid of waste from its body.» The words get rid of waste from its body tell you that defecate means to pass waste out of the body.
explain: Clues can also come from a sign or a list. «Do not allow your dog to defecate here» is a park sign. Dogs do not read signs, so the sign is for owners, and it asks them to clean up after their dogs. Now you know defecate is about the waste a dog leaves behind.
explain: Formal words often have everyday partners. In everyday talk, people say «go for a poo» or «go to the toilet». Defecate means the same thing, but it is the word used in science, health leaflets and by doctors. You will meet it more often when you read about the body.
fact: Defecate is a verb, so it describes an action.
fact: «Defecate» means to pass solid waste, or poo, out of the body through the bottom.
fact: Its other forms are defecates, defecated and defecating.
fact: In science, getting rid of waste is one of the life processes, and defecating is part of this.
fact: Doctors and health leaflets use the word defecate, while everyday talk uses words like «go for a poo».
exercise: «Every animal must defecate to get rid of waste from its body.» What does defecate mean? | To go for a long walk | *To pass solid waste out of the body | To grow new teeth | To drink plenty of water
exercise: A park sign says «do not allow your dog to defecate here». What is the sign asking? | Please feed the dogs on the grass | Dogs are allowed to run and play here | *Please do not let your dog leave solid waste on the grass | Please keep the park tidy by picking up litter
exercise: Which everyday phrase means the same as defecate? | go for a walk | *go for a poo | go to bed | go for a swim
test: «The doctor asked Sam how often he defecated.» What does defecated mean here? | *Passed solid waste out of his body | Went to school | Ran quickly to the toilet | Felt very hungry
test: «In science we learned that getting rid of waste, when we defecate, is one of the life processes.» What is the topic of this sentence? | *Waste leaving the body | Sleeping and dreaming | Reading stories | Playing sport
exam: Defecate is a verb. Which form shows that the action happened in the past? | defecates | defecate | *defecated | defecating
